1
00:00:08,926 --> 00:00:12,221
Baek-hee's mung bean <i>jeon</i>
is better than yours.

2
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:15,015
It's good. Why don't you eat?

3
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:20,229
Mother, you told me 30 years ago

4
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:24,691
that family forms as people collide,
mix together, and become one.

5
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,319
Even after my husband died

6
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:30,322
I always thought this was
where I belonged.

7
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:33,116
"I'd better do my best
as a daughter-in-law."

8
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,496
Because it was the family I chose.

9
00:00:40,207 --> 00:00:41,917
Yes, I know that.

10
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:47,047
But you know what, Mother and Father.

11
00:00:47,798 --> 00:00:50,509
I think I'm going to take a step back
as a daughter-in-law

12
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:54,846
and take a step forward as a mother.

13
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,056
What do you mean?

14
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:58,141
I'm going to give

15
00:00:59,226 --> 00:01:00,894
Yeon-su and Mr. Dokgo Dal
my blessing.

16
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:08,402
- Baek-hee.
- Yeon-su would never act rashly.

17
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:12,948
I'm going to trust her.

18
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:16,285
Because she's my daughter.

19
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:36,972
- Who is it?
- Se-ra.

20
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:38,473
It's me, Yeon-su's mom.

21
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,227
Ms. Seo, what brings you here
at this hour?

22
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:44,730
I'm sorry to bother you so late.

23
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,690
I couldn't get ahold of Yeon-su.

24
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:49,860
She must've emptied your fridge.

25
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:51,653
I made you some side dishes.

26
00:01:51,737 --> 00:01:52,821
Right.

27
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:55,032
Sorry about the hassle.
I appreciate it.

28
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:57,075
The hassle?

29
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:00,746
Oh, yes. Right.

30
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,331
Thank you for the food.

31
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:06,168
We had nothing to eat at home,
so she went out to buy fried chicken.

32
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:07,878
Let me call her...

33
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,840
Is she not here?

34
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,008
Well...

35
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:18,805
Se-ra?

36
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:22,934
What's she doing here?

37
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:29,524
Se-ra, what brings you here?

38
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:36,990
Mom...

39
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,197
Mom.

40
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,533
I can explain.

41
00:03:26,832 --> 00:03:27,916
Mom.

42
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,252
Mom.

43
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:33,422
Did you defy the elders
and leave home

44
00:03:33,839 --> 00:03:34,923
just to move in with a man?

45
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:36,550
Is that why you left home?

46
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:39,010
It's not like that.

47
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:41,012
I'm only staying here temporarily.

48
00:03:41,096 --> 00:03:42,723
Is this how you grow your feelings?

49
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:47,561
Gong Yeon-su,
I'm really disappointed.

50
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:53,275
I'll drive you home.

51
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:00,782
Get in.

52
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:03,785
Get in now!

53
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,093
I'm not leaving, Mom.

54
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:26,433
I'm going to stay here
until I find a place of my own.

55
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:29,811
Take care, Mom.

56
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:36,067
- Se-ra, please drive my mom home.
- Okay.

57
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:56,254
MAKE ME TINGLE

58
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,577
What are you doing?

59
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:29,287
Are you up?

60
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:31,164
Get ready for breakfast.
It's soy sauce and egg rice.

61
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,919
Wait. You said
you don't eat breakfast, right?

62
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:38,004
Then why don't you
just have a little taste?

63
00:05:49,975 --> 00:05:50,976
Are you okay?

64
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:53,436
What do you mean?

65
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,397
You didn't seem
to get any sleep last night.

66
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:00,944
I'm going to check out
some houses today.

67
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:03,154
I hope I find something good.

68
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,282
Have you really made up your mind?

69
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,200
Yes.

70
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,996
What? Do I look hopeless?

71
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:12,998
That's not what I meant.

72
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:18,003
I had to face it eventually anyway.

73
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:21,006
I'm jumping over the fence
I've lived behind my whole life.

74
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:22,799
Well...

75
00:06:23,425 --> 00:06:25,260
I'm bound
to get at least a scratch somewhere.

76
00:06:30,265 --> 00:06:32,100
FINAL EPISODE

77
00:06:37,689 --> 00:06:39,065
What a brat.

78
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:43,653
If an elder takes a step back,
she should thank you and come home.

79
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:46,865
This is why people say
there's no point raising daughters.

80
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:48,617
Why is my ear so itchy?

81
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:52,245
Baek-hee, you should talk to her.

82
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:56,499
Tell her she can date him
while living with her family.

83
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:00,378
Nam-su, you too.

84
00:07:00,462 --> 00:07:02,714
Once your exam is over,
I'll arrange a blind date for you.

85
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,383
With Professor Um's second daughter?

86
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:06,968
Isn't she
an elementary school teacher?

87
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:10,305
What's the rush?

88
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:13,183
We should wait for the result
before you do anything...

89
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:15,018
- What result?
- We should consider

90
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,145
- her preference.
- Shut it!

91
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,438
How can it get any better

92
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,649
than a Grade Seven civil servant
with his face?

93
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:22,275
- That's true.
- Well...

94
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:24,986
- Grandfather.
- Yes?

95
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:31,201
I want to postpone my exam
for a year.

96
00:07:34,663 --> 00:07:35,997
- What?
- Nam-su.

97
00:07:36,498 --> 00:07:38,416
Don't be like this.

98
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:41,419
People say when you're distracted,
you lose your edge.

99
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:46,174
I want to spend a year
to settle down...

100
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:49,094
Don't you care about your mom
who's supporting you?

101
00:07:49,511 --> 00:07:50,804
Distracted?

102
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:52,639
Are you sure it's not your head
that's distracted?

103
00:07:56,685 --> 00:07:57,686
Nam-su.

104
00:07:58,937 --> 00:08:00,772
If you don't pass this time

105
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:03,817
you should leave too.

106
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:06,027
Don't be like that.

107
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:08,697
I don't need anyone who defies me.

108
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,991
If you want to do it your way,
get out of my house.

109
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:14,202
Can I?

110
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:19,499
Are you saying I can move out
and live on my own?

111
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:21,167
Live on your own?

112
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:26,381
Are you all looking to move out?

113
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:29,050
- Baek-hee.
- Yes.

114
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:30,343
Clear the table.

115
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:32,387
No.

116
00:08:32,721 --> 00:08:35,598
It's about time
to paint some orchids.

117
00:08:37,684 --> 00:08:39,060
Grandfather.

118
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:57,579
Grandfather, when are you going
to start painting?

119
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:07,797
The ink is too watery.

120
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:20,101
Dal.

121
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:23,396
Aren't you basically a traitor
to her family?

122
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,024
What did Yeon-su say?

123
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:29,277
It seems she's made up her mind
to move out.

124
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:34,783
- So you are a traitor.
- Whether I'm a traitor or a thief

125
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:37,702
I don't care.

126
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:42,290
I'm just worried she'll grow distant
from her family because of me.

127
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:45,877
Don't blame yourself.

128
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:50,048
Fine. Let's say she grows distant.

129
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:51,925
But that's her choice.

130
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:54,719
You shouldn't feel guilty about it.
You're both adults.

131
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,596
When you're in love

132
00:09:56,679 --> 00:10:00,391
you do things you never did before
and make decisions on impulse.

133
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,853
Both you and Yeon-su are the same.

134
00:10:04,479 --> 00:10:05,772
- Me?
- Yes.

135
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,398
That's what you're doing right now.

136
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:10,318
- I am?
- You can't bear to stay with anyone

137
00:10:10,401 --> 00:10:11,569
that you even kick me out.

138
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,405
But how long has it been
since she moved in with you?

139
00:10:14,489 --> 00:10:15,782
Isn't it uncomfortable?

140
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,033
Doesn't she get on your nerves?

141
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:19,202
Oh, jeez.

142
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:20,662
I'm really disappointed, you know?

143
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,664
Tell me. Is it me or Yeon-su?

144
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:25,458
- Obviously...
- No, I don't want to hear it.

145
00:10:27,502 --> 00:10:29,629
Actually, say it.

146
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:31,506
I can handle it.

147
00:10:32,841 --> 00:10:35,552
- Really?
- Your eyebrows just answered me.

148
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:36,636
Let's go.

149
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:39,973
- Where are you going?
- To eat.

150
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:43,017
- I'm not eating.
- Why won't you eat?

151
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:45,311
Do you not like it?
Do you want something else?

152
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:47,480
No, it's okay.

153
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:50,108
I'm really fine, Se-ra.

154
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,569
But I feel so bad.

155
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:56,531
Do you know how much I prayed
for the door to stay closed that day?

156
00:10:56,656 --> 00:11:00,785
By the way, how did you know
where he lived?

157
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:02,787
- What?
- Aside from work

158
00:11:02,871 --> 00:11:04,539
there's no link between you two.

159
00:11:05,165 --> 00:11:06,457
The thing is

160
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,587
there is one link
that you're not aware of.

161
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,547
A link I'm not aware of?

162
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:19,679
- What?
- I didn't mean to hide it.

163
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:22,473
As you already know,
I talk about their existence

164
00:11:22,557 --> 00:11:24,184
but I never reveal who they are.

165
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:25,852
Oh, wow.

166
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:28,229
No wonder you left me alone in Busan.

167
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:30,690
So you were with Min-hyung all along?

168
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:35,320
Come on.
It's not like you were alone.

169
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:38,323
Is it over between you two now?

170
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:41,242
He did graduate for now.

171
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,745
- For now?
- <i>Se-ra.</i>

172
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:45,246
Now that I've graduated

173
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:47,165
how about we get to know each other?

174
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,083
What's there to know?

175
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:50,835
How scary a younger guy...

176
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,755
who suddenly discovered
the fun can be.

177
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:58,426
You know I'm not into relationships.

178
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:01,930
You must be aware
I'm only into casual dating too.

179
00:12:02,347 --> 00:12:04,432
<i>Should I call it</i>
<i>long-term casual dating?</i>

180
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:09,145
Right. You don't need to define
a relationship as dating.

181
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:13,733
- Yeon-su, what's gotten into you?
- What do you mean?

182
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:16,319
"You might
as well go out with him, Se-ra."

183
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:17,528
Why aren't you saying that?

184
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,407
I can't tell you what to do.

185
00:12:21,491 --> 00:12:23,534
There's no right answer
to relationships.

186
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:25,870
Se-ra, try this. This is good.

187
00:12:31,668 --> 00:12:34,295
Si-eun, where are you?

188
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:43,805
SEON-HUI'S

189
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,609
- That's hot.
<i>- Are you okay?</i>

190
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,403
<i>Are you hurt?</i>

191
00:12:59,696 --> 00:13:01,739
Si-eun, stay away from the fire.

192
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:02,824
I'll grill it.

193
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:08,955
That looks good.

194
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:15,169
Try this.

195
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,629
I bet it's super tender.

196
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:21,009
- Is it good?
- It's so good. I love it.

197
00:13:21,092 --> 00:13:22,093
Try this next.

198
00:13:27,682 --> 00:13:30,018
- Good?
- You should eat too.

199
00:13:30,101 --> 00:13:31,227
You're giving me everything.

200
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:33,604
I don't know
why it's so fun to feed you.

201
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:37,150
<i>- Good.</i>
<i>- I know, right?</i>

202
00:13:52,415 --> 00:13:53,875
<i>Why does this taste so good?</i>

203
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:13,770
1-ON-1 INQUIRY

204
00:14:13,853 --> 00:14:16,439
WILL THIS HELP OUR INTIMACY?

205
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:23,029
<i>Have you given it to your wife?</i>

206
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:24,489
<i>I'm sorry</i>

207
00:14:24,781 --> 00:14:26,783
<i>but it's unused. Can I get a refund?</i>

208
00:14:27,075 --> 00:14:28,284
A refund?

209
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:30,536
<i>I barely plucked up</i>
<i>my courage to buy it</i>

210
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:32,872
<i>but I don't have the courage</i>
<i>to use it.</i>

211
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:35,583
<i>Do you have</i>

212
00:14:36,209 --> 00:14:40,046
<i>the courage to talk to your wife?</i>

213
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:47,887
<i>I don't know.</i>
<i>Maybe one day when I get a chance.</i>

214
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,357
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Let's do it now.

215
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:01,025
What are you saying?

216
00:15:01,109 --> 00:15:04,904
You said maybe one day.
When's that going to be?

217
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:07,490
<i>We might as well do it now.</i>

218
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:09,867
Let's pluck up our courage.

219
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:15,665
I'll wait for you at the place
we used to go.

220
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:18,000
I DON'T KNOW
MAYBE ONE DAY WHEN I GET A CHANCE

221
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:25,007
Since when?

222
00:15:25,091 --> 00:15:26,634
When was it...

223
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:33,182
Around the time
when you quit your job.

224
00:16:05,882 --> 00:16:07,216
You're not going to return it,
are you?

225
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:16,767
Don't be so cheap.

226
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,388
What's taking her so long?

227
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:58,601
I should've gone to pick her up.

228
00:17:00,895 --> 00:17:01,979
There she is.

229
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,151
Hi.

230
00:17:07,235 --> 00:17:09,320
You scared me.
Are you going somewhere?

231
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:11,906
- No.
- Why are you standing there?

232
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,741
To get water.

233
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,244
By the gate?

234
00:17:19,956 --> 00:17:21,749
Where's your other shoe?

235
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:36,973
Did you get to see any places?

236
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,433
I saw a few,
but I need to see a few more.

237
00:17:40,268 --> 00:17:42,812
Did you see anything near here,
by any chance?

238
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:44,105
Near your house?

239
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:46,190
This is a good neighborhood.

240
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,067
It has everything you need.

241
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:54,574
But the price isn't so good.

242
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:02,039
- Where are you going?
- I'm getting water.

243
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:03,499
I'll get it for you.

244
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:08,045
- Lukewarm water, please.
- Okay.

245
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:17,805
Wait, where are you going?

246
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:19,849
Tissue.

247
00:18:29,567 --> 00:18:30,568
What?

248
00:18:32,153 --> 00:18:34,864
I just noticed you're kind of clingy.

249
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:36,907
No, I'm not.

250
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:39,744
Yes, you are.

251
00:18:44,665 --> 00:18:45,958
I like it.

252
00:18:46,042 --> 00:18:48,878
When I was asked where I was
or where I was going my whole life

253
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,713
it felt like nagging.

254
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:55,885
But now I don't have
to hear that anymore.

255
00:18:59,347 --> 00:19:00,389
But

256
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:05,561
I don't want you to lose
anything precious because of me.

257
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:08,856
- Anything precious?
- For example

258
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:10,816
turning your back on your family.

259
00:19:12,652 --> 00:19:14,654
Did I turn my back on my family?

260
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:19,492
I did take a few steps back,
but I never turned my back on them.

261
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:23,746
No? But you're here with me
after you left home over a fight.

262
00:19:31,921 --> 00:19:34,715
I like you, Mr. Dokgo.

263
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:38,761
But the reason I left home is

264
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,013
because I'm finally strong enough

265
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,599
to stand by my own choices
without being swayed.

266
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:45,476
Because I want

267
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:47,895
to set standards for myself,
not have them set by anyone else.

268
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:51,357
I want to be responsible
for my own life.

269
00:19:57,822 --> 00:20:04,120
So stop feeling guilty
and just tell me I'll do fine.

270
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:12,002
What is it?

271
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:16,424
Nothing.

272
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,217
You're so pretty.

273
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:26,392
Stop it.

274
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:43,576
Oh, what?

275
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,830
I'll give you one more chance.

276
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:00,509
MY SI-EUN

277
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,263
Where are you?

278
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:20,029
Kang Si-eun!

279
00:21:26,202 --> 00:21:27,369
Nam-su.

280
00:21:30,206 --> 00:21:31,457
Why, you...

281
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:35,044
I'm sorry.

282
00:21:36,337 --> 00:21:37,379
I really am.

283
00:21:39,882 --> 00:21:41,342
I can't give up on dancing.

284
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:45,012
But I can't give up
on the baby either.

285
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:48,766
- Si-eun.
- Why do I have to choose one?

286
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:51,936
I can't give up on my dream
for the baby

287
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:53,312
or the baby for my dream.

288
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:55,397
I might pull off both. Who knows?

289
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:57,024
Am I wrong?

290
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:58,526
I've made up my mind.

291
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:02,571
- This is my answer.
- Can I talk now?

292
00:22:03,614 --> 00:22:04,615
Yes.

293
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:09,537
Si-eun, there is an old saying,
<i>"Dongsimjieon yujigyeongseong."</i>

294
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,790
"Words spoken with one heart
make a way.

295
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:13,999
And where there is a will..."

296
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:15,167
- Nam-su.
- Yes?

297
00:22:15,501 --> 00:22:16,502
Keep it simple.

298
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:19,296
I love you.

299
00:22:24,552 --> 00:22:28,305
- Nam-su, I got burned here.
- What? How?

300
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:31,767
- The clam popped.
- Oh, no. Doesn't it hurt?

301
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,561
- It does.
- It does?

302
00:22:37,857 --> 00:22:41,735
Why are you packing so much?
It'll be heavy.

303
00:22:42,444 --> 00:22:44,572
Your brother liked rice cakes.

304
00:22:45,281 --> 00:22:48,158
You must be the only wife
who still celebrates

305
00:22:48,242 --> 00:22:49,952
her wedding anniversary every year

306
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:52,872
with her children
even after her husband died.

307
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,040
Where are they, anyway?

308
00:22:57,167 --> 00:22:59,837
I wonder what it would've been like
if he were still alive.

309
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:03,924
He would've disciplined the kids
big time.

310
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:05,593
But then who knows?

311
00:23:05,676 --> 00:23:09,054
He might have
let Yeon-su get away with it.

312
00:23:09,138 --> 00:23:12,600
You know he was always soft
when it came to Yeon-su.

313
00:23:12,683 --> 00:23:13,851
I don't know.

314
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:18,606
If he were alive
this wouldn't have happened.

315
00:23:18,689 --> 00:23:19,940
You never know.

316
00:23:20,024 --> 00:23:21,817
Look at my life
even though my dad is still alive.

317
00:23:23,736 --> 00:23:26,196
Please take care of their meal later.

318
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:28,699
Don't worry about it.

319
00:23:30,784 --> 00:23:33,203
Mother and Father, I'm leaving now.

320
00:23:34,330 --> 00:23:37,249
- I think I'll order pizza for lunch.
- Sure.

321
00:24:04,193 --> 00:24:06,403
<i>I have something important to do,</i>
<i>so I'm heading out first.</i>

322
00:24:06,487 --> 00:24:07,821
<i>Make sure to eat.</i>

323
00:24:13,327 --> 00:24:14,912
- Hello?
- Where are you?

324
00:24:14,995 --> 00:24:16,080
<i>Home, obviously.</i>

325
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:18,332
- Are you home alone?
- Why do you want to know?

326
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:20,542
I got a call
from Yeon-su's grandfather.

327
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:22,920
<i>He said the house feels empty.</i>

328
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:24,755
<i>He wants me to play Go with him.</i>

329
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:27,925
- So?
<i>- I said yes.</i>

330
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:30,386
- Hey, Yun Ji-o...
- But I didn't say who was going.

331
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:32,680
- What?
<i>- I'm just saying.</i>

332
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:34,181
Bye.

333
00:24:47,194 --> 00:24:48,737
Long time no see, Dad.

334
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:56,745
I guess I'm the first one here.

335
00:24:58,539 --> 00:25:01,667
You need to understand
even if everyone comes

336
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,378
separately this year.

337
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:26,942
Father, we're getting marriage offers
for both Yeon-su and Nam-su.

338
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:29,695
But what about my remarriage?

339
00:25:32,406 --> 00:25:34,950
Do you even want to do it?

340
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:37,161
If you do, I'll look into it.

341
00:25:37,244 --> 00:25:39,997
It's not just that I want it.
It's all I think about all day long.

342
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:42,249
I mean, I'm still young.

343
00:25:42,332 --> 00:25:43,667
I need to meet someone.

344
00:25:43,751 --> 00:25:46,670
- A woman turning 50 isn't young.
- I'm not 50 yet!

345
00:25:46,754 --> 00:25:50,340
If I try hard,
I can still get pregnant.

346
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:53,635
Neither of your grandchildren
has a choice.

347
00:25:53,719 --> 00:25:56,013
Should I get you a new grandchild?

348
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:57,097
- Oh, jeez.
- Oh, jeez.

349
00:26:02,186 --> 00:26:05,230
- Why do you keep coming here?
- I'm here to learn Go.

350
00:26:05,314 --> 00:26:07,691
I'm glad you're here.

351
00:26:07,775 --> 00:26:10,235
We were having lunch.
Come and join us.

352
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:13,030
- Mi-young.
- Yes.

353
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:15,240
Clear the table.

354
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:31,006
You must have a lot of free time
on your hands.

355
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,592
Is your adult toy business slow?

356
00:26:33,675 --> 00:26:36,428
It's doing great.
I've got capable staff

357
00:26:36,512 --> 00:26:38,222
so the company
practically runs itself.

358
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:40,432
You always have to have
the last word, don't you?

359
00:26:41,016 --> 00:26:43,602
Are you talking
to Yeon-su these days?

360
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:48,190
She's never caused us
this much grief before.

361
00:26:49,316 --> 00:26:51,026
Our ancestor from six generations ago

362
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:54,321
received a royal decree of chastity
during the reign of King Jeongjo.

363
00:26:54,655 --> 00:26:56,990
That's not all. Our ancestor
from four generations ago

364
00:26:57,074 --> 00:26:59,243
had a monument of virtue
erected by the village of Seocheon.

365
00:27:00,327 --> 00:27:03,372
And now some scoundrel
has completely ruined it all.

366
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:05,040
Jeez.

367
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:07,751
Ms. Gong is simply

368
00:27:08,168 --> 00:27:10,754
taking the next step forward
in her life.

369
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,925
- What?
- It honestly stings a bit

370
00:27:15,008 --> 00:27:16,135
since I take second place there.

371
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:20,097
But that's exactly why I like her.

372
00:27:24,810 --> 00:27:29,106
I deeply respect
how strong and principled she is.

373
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:33,986
Her belief in herself, her values,
and her manners.

374
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:38,866
She has this unique integrity
you don't see in other people.

375
00:27:39,533 --> 00:27:43,370
She must've learned it
from her grandparents.

376
00:27:47,624 --> 00:27:51,628
Not for a single moment
have I ever taken her for granted.

377
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:53,213
Oh, my.

378
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:04,474
- What are you doing? Keep grinding.
- Oh, right.

379
00:28:22,993 --> 00:28:25,704
At least, you're good
at grinding the ink.

380
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,294
<i>I'll take my leave now.</i>

381
00:28:36,465 --> 00:28:38,342
Come visit us again.

382
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:41,720
Oh, and I have something to tell you.

383
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:43,555
Would you lean for a second?

384
00:28:47,476 --> 00:28:48,477
Truth is...

385
00:28:54,191 --> 00:28:58,570
- I'll be on my way, then.
- Take care.

386
00:29:09,206 --> 00:29:11,250
- You're not bad.
- I'm sorry?

387
00:29:11,333 --> 00:29:13,001
My father drew orchids.

388
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:17,464
It's just a thing. You'd better learn
how to play Go in advance.

389
00:29:18,048 --> 00:29:19,967
Actually, no. Don't even bother.

390
00:29:20,717 --> 00:29:22,761
- It'll only get exhausting.
- By the way

391
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:24,346
I don't see Ms. Gong's mother.

392
00:29:24,721 --> 00:29:26,640
- Did she go somewhere?
- Oh, her.

393
00:29:27,975 --> 00:29:31,186
Today marks a certain anniversary.
She went to visit my brother's grave.

394
00:29:31,270 --> 00:29:32,354
Did Yeon-su not tell you?

395
00:29:37,234 --> 00:29:40,279
I've looked into a few places.

396
00:29:40,529 --> 00:29:42,864
About 15 minutes from home.

397
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:45,993
It's got to be close
so we can see each other often.

398
00:29:49,162 --> 00:29:51,290
Nothing's really going to change.

399
00:29:51,373 --> 00:29:54,710
I'll be there
for all holidays, birthdays

400
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,962
Parents' Day, and memorial services.

401
00:29:57,045 --> 00:29:59,381
I'll keep in touch frequently too.

402
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:04,011
Yeon-su.

403
00:30:07,889 --> 00:30:09,224
Let me ask you just one thing.

404
00:30:12,477 --> 00:30:14,438
Were you lonely

405
00:30:16,315 --> 00:30:17,566
during your time in this house?

406
00:30:28,410 --> 00:30:31,663
That's unfair for you to ask me that.

407
00:30:34,041 --> 00:30:35,250
Who else in this house

408
00:30:37,127 --> 00:30:39,421
could have been as lonely as you?

409
00:30:45,594 --> 00:30:46,762
But you must know.

410
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:51,266
It was all my choice.

411
00:30:52,142 --> 00:30:53,268
INSTALLMENT SAVINGS PASSBOOK

412
00:30:56,229 --> 00:30:59,608
Three years is enough.
You've done your duty, Baek-hee.

413
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:04,863
Don't waste your youth
taking care of us old folks anymore.

414
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:07,449
Go out and live your own life.

415
00:31:10,494 --> 00:31:14,331
It breaks my heart
to hear you say that.

416
00:31:15,665 --> 00:31:17,376
Father, Mother.

417
00:31:17,459 --> 00:31:19,544
You're the very first family
I ever chose.

418
00:31:20,337 --> 00:31:22,506
Regardless of my husband's presence

419
00:31:23,215 --> 00:31:24,424
I'm staying

420
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:27,594
as your daughter-in-law
and as part of this family.

421
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:31,098
<i>I sure was lonely</i>

422
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:33,975
but it wasn't all that bad.

423
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,646
My decision to stay in this house

424
00:31:38,063 --> 00:31:39,231
wasn't out of obligation.

425
00:31:39,773 --> 00:31:40,982
It was out of love.

426
00:31:44,569 --> 00:31:45,779
I wanted to raise you kids

427
00:31:46,613 --> 00:31:49,282
in a safe family environment.

428
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,286
Little did I know

429
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:56,373
that very environment
would end up becoming a cage.

430
00:31:56,706 --> 00:32:02,879
Mom, remember what you told me
when you pinned my hair up at 20?

431
00:32:04,005 --> 00:32:07,384
<i>This </i>binyeo <i>represents</i>
<i>the responsibility you hold</i>

432
00:32:08,176 --> 00:32:09,803
<i>as a woman.</i>

433
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:13,265
<i>From now on, you must carry</i>
<i>your body and mind</i>

434
00:32:13,557 --> 00:32:15,976
<i>with dignity and care.</i>

435
00:32:17,227 --> 00:32:21,440
That <i>binyeo </i>felt so heavy back then.

436
00:32:25,861 --> 00:32:29,114
But looking back,
I believe that weight is

437
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:31,700
what kept me from faltering.

438
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:38,290
You weren't putting us in a cage.

439
00:32:38,373 --> 00:32:39,541
You were protecting us.

440
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:41,084
It's just

441
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:44,087
we've grown enough to survive

442
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:47,174
without that fence now. That's all.

443
00:32:48,008 --> 00:32:52,429
Just as you followed
your heart back then

444
00:32:54,055 --> 00:32:57,434
I'm going to start following mine.

445
00:33:00,604 --> 00:33:02,772
I didn't fully realize

446
00:33:04,191 --> 00:33:06,776
that you grew up this well.

447
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:10,530
Of course.

448
00:33:11,615 --> 00:33:13,116
I'm your pride, after all.

449
00:33:18,163 --> 00:33:19,372
Did you hear that, honey?

450
00:33:27,297 --> 00:33:31,510
GONG SEOK-JUN'S GRAVE

451
00:33:33,887 --> 00:33:36,681
- It's raining.
- Why the sudden rain?

452
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:41,019
Your dad's probably throwing a fit
because Nam-su didn't show up.

453
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:42,729
Right?

454
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:44,773
Goodness.

455
00:33:47,067 --> 00:33:48,902
It's pouring quite heavily.
Mom, be careful.

456
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:51,780
- Gosh, it's raining so suddenly.
- Mom, hand that to me.

457
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:54,157
- It's okay. It's fine.
- No, it's heavy.

458
00:33:57,244 --> 00:33:58,578
Mr. Dokgo?

459
00:34:01,331 --> 00:34:02,791
Let's head to the car first.

460
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:04,793
- Please hand it over.
- It's fine, though.

461
00:34:14,386 --> 00:34:16,137
How did you know we were here?

462
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:18,640
Your aunt told me.

463
00:34:18,974 --> 00:34:21,142
- You visited our house?
- Yes.

464
00:34:22,978 --> 00:34:25,063
Are you cold? Do you want a blanket?

465
00:34:25,146 --> 00:34:27,023
I'm all right. I have one.

466
00:34:28,275 --> 00:34:29,526
- Oh, my.
- What is it?

467
00:34:30,485 --> 00:34:33,113
- Don't tell me you left it behind.
- Yes, I totally left it.

468
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:34,364
Oh, no.

469
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:36,157
- I'll go and grab it.
- No.

470
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:38,451
- I'll go.
- Oh, no.

471
00:34:38,535 --> 00:34:40,662
You don't know where it is.
I'll be back in a flash.

472
00:34:41,580 --> 00:34:43,540
Then, let's go together.

473
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:45,542
Okay.

474
00:35:24,581 --> 00:35:26,166
So this is why you made it pour.

475
00:35:28,543 --> 00:35:31,630
He's the spitting image
of you in your youth.

476
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:45,852
Jeez, why is it
suddenly raining again?

477
00:35:50,607 --> 00:35:52,233
Did something good happen?

478
00:35:52,317 --> 00:35:54,611
It's none of your business.

479
00:35:58,198 --> 00:36:00,367
Truth is, I don't shoot blanks.

480
00:36:09,250 --> 00:36:11,753
I'm Lee Yu-ri of Brand Planning
at Hyunseong Department Store.

481
00:36:12,253 --> 00:36:13,463
LEE YU-RI

482
00:36:13,546 --> 00:36:15,465
I'm Yun Ji-o,
Vice President of Loand.

483
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:24,015
Since it's a test store,
early reactions are everything.

484
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:26,601
Customer feedback goes straight
into our internal reviews.

485
00:36:26,685 --> 00:36:30,105
So the opening week will be
basically our report card.

486
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:32,482
- I'm sure we can pull it off.
- One thing, though.

487
00:36:32,565 --> 00:36:34,567
The term pressure
might struggle to pass the review

488
00:36:34,651 --> 00:36:36,528
due to its underlying nuance.

489
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:38,446
Even so, could you still submit it
for review?

490
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:40,699
If it gets rejected,
we'll proceed with Plan B.

491
00:36:40,782 --> 00:36:43,910
The email you sent me
even had Plan C.

492
00:36:43,993 --> 00:36:46,162
Only the promotional keywords
extend to Plan C.

493
00:36:46,246 --> 00:36:49,874
The product lists and interior drafts
go all the way to Plan F.

494
00:36:51,376 --> 00:36:53,044
Are you an ENFJ by any chance?

495
00:36:53,128 --> 00:36:55,588
Spot on. Are you an ENFJ too?

496
00:36:55,672 --> 00:36:58,133
Yes, I'm also an ENFJ.

497
00:36:59,384 --> 00:37:00,677
What a coincidence.

498
00:37:01,636 --> 00:37:03,054
Should we grab a bite first?

499
00:37:03,138 --> 00:37:04,889
- Mr. Dokgo.
- Sounds good.

500
00:37:04,973 --> 00:37:06,850
- Please review the agency's drafts.
- Yes?

501
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:11,646
Hello? Hi, honey.

502
00:37:11,980 --> 00:37:13,648
- Yes.
- My stomach suddenly...

503
00:37:14,107 --> 00:37:16,359
You're hungry? I see.

504
00:37:18,445 --> 00:37:21,030
- What kind of food do you like?
- I eat pretty much everything.

505
00:37:21,114 --> 00:37:22,907
Except for one thing.

506
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:25,660
- Sumac chicken.
- Really? Same here.

507
00:37:25,744 --> 00:37:26,995
Really?

508
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:29,581
I actually ended up in the ER once
after eating it.

509
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:32,167
<i>No way. Me too. I got all swollen.</i>

510
00:37:44,345 --> 00:37:45,930
How's the Hyunseong launch going?

511
00:37:46,014 --> 00:37:47,599
Where did you hear about that?

512
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,392
It's not anything classified,
you know.

513
00:37:49,476 --> 00:37:50,643
It's still in the works.

514
00:37:52,562 --> 00:37:53,772
Are you still living with that girl?

515
00:37:56,775 --> 00:37:57,859
Did you guys split up?

516
00:37:59,194 --> 00:38:01,780
- No.
- I can't believe you let a woman in.

517
00:38:02,489 --> 00:38:04,073
She must really be something.

518
00:38:04,157 --> 00:38:07,076
After all that talk about not wanting
to hurt the people precious to you.

519
00:38:09,454 --> 00:38:11,039
Don't give me that look.

520
00:38:11,456 --> 00:38:13,666
I'm not hating. I'm just curious.

521
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:21,466
I'm going to try not to hurt her.

522
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:25,970
I want to make an effort this time.

523
00:38:31,601 --> 00:38:32,602
Rest assured.

524
00:38:33,937 --> 00:38:35,396
You're nothing like me.

525
00:38:36,105 --> 00:38:39,067
At least, you won't be
the kind of parent

526
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,777
who shops around
for an adequate mother

527
00:38:41,778 --> 00:38:42,987
for his child.

528
00:38:47,951 --> 00:38:49,577
The kid has this darkness to him.

529
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:51,788
He's got such a cold look in his eyes
for someone so young.

530
00:38:53,039 --> 00:38:54,040
DIVORCE REGISTRATION

531
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:56,125
<i>He can feed himself well enough.</i>

532
00:38:56,209 --> 00:38:58,211
<i>I didn't get married</i>
<i>just to prepare his meals.</i>

533
00:38:58,294 --> 00:39:00,213
<i>I'll have to see how he behaves.</i>

534
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:03,508
You didn't already transfer
your assets to him, did you?

535
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:06,886
Give him a call
and tell him to come eat.

536
00:39:09,013 --> 00:39:10,181
It's his birthday, after all.

537
00:39:10,682 --> 00:39:12,392
Forget it. That's unnecessary.

538
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:24,863
Eat up.
You're paying the bill, anyway.

539
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:26,614
- I am?
- Of course, you should pay.

540
00:39:26,698 --> 00:39:27,824
You're rolling in cash these days.

541
00:39:29,117 --> 00:39:30,952
Have you tried her cooking,
by the way?

542
00:39:31,244 --> 00:39:32,287
She's an amazing cook.

543
00:39:33,621 --> 00:39:36,916
Is that so?
All right, it's on me today.

544
00:39:37,917 --> 00:39:39,711
- You sure?
- Yes.

545
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:43,047
Look at my boy, all grown up.

546
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:46,092
Could you bring it over here?

547
00:39:48,094 --> 00:39:49,888
You may place it right here.

548
00:39:50,138 --> 00:39:51,389
A little more to this side.

549
00:40:05,904 --> 00:40:07,030
Hi, Se-ra.

550
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:09,324
<i>How does it feel</i>
<i>to be out on your own?</i>

551
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:11,367
It's great.

552
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:12,660
It really is, but...

553
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,790
You should've put this down gently.

554
00:40:17,874 --> 00:40:19,250
It's all shattered.

555
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:22,003
Maybe I moved
a little too close to home.

556
00:40:22,879 --> 00:40:24,505
<i>What do you want</i>
<i>for a housewarming gift?</i>

557
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:26,716
Anything's fine.

558
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:29,886
- Thanks.
<i>- All right, I'll hit you up later.</i>

559
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:35,308
<i>On the day of the first snowfall</i>

560
00:40:35,391 --> 00:40:38,811
<i>I got a space to call my own</i>
<i>for the first time in my life.</i>

561
00:40:39,437 --> 00:40:40,855
Wait. I got a cramp.

562
00:40:40,939 --> 00:40:43,107
A cramp? Where? Here?

563
00:40:43,191 --> 00:40:44,776
Just kidding.

564
00:40:44,859 --> 00:40:48,321
<i>Se-ra continued</i>
<i>her endless situationship.</i>

565
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:51,449
PREGNANCY JOURNAL

566
00:40:52,784 --> 00:40:54,661
BABY CRIB

567
00:40:56,079 --> 00:40:57,830
Be careful.

568
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:03,628
CIVIL SERVANT ID
GONG NAM-SU

569
00:41:04,128 --> 00:41:06,005
Is the crib too small?

570
00:41:06,089 --> 00:41:07,632
Too small? Should I swap it
for a bigger one?

571
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:09,258
It feels a bit too low.

572
00:41:09,342 --> 00:41:10,927
Too low? Should I replace it
with a taller one?

573
00:41:11,636 --> 00:41:13,638
I really can't say a single thing
around you.

574
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:15,181
My dear.

575
00:41:15,264 --> 00:41:16,891
Make Nam-su do all of this.

576
00:41:16,975 --> 00:41:20,520
Sit right down here

577
00:41:20,603 --> 00:41:23,064
- and have this.
- Thank you.

578
00:41:25,566 --> 00:41:26,818
Where's Grandpa?

579
00:41:26,901 --> 00:41:29,070
He went to the market
to buy some clams for her.

580
00:41:30,113 --> 00:41:32,740
<i>The day Nam-su dropped the bomb</i>
<i>that he was going to be a dad...</i>

581
00:41:32,824 --> 00:41:35,660
What? A dad?

582
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:41,749
Good heavens!

583
00:41:41,833 --> 00:41:43,167
- Father!
- Grandfather!

584
00:41:43,251 --> 00:41:44,794
Call an ambulance!

585
00:41:44,877 --> 00:41:45,920
<i>- Grandpa passed out</i>
- Ambulance.

586
00:41:46,004 --> 00:41:47,296
- Grandpa.
<i>- from a blood pressure spike.</i>

587
00:41:47,380 --> 00:41:48,673
- Oh, no.
- Wake up.

588
00:41:49,590 --> 00:41:51,592
<i>And fortunately...</i>

589
00:41:52,093 --> 00:41:53,219
It's a boy.

590
00:41:55,304 --> 00:41:57,098
A boy?

591
00:42:01,769 --> 00:42:04,689
- Baek-hee, get me some water.
- Yes, Father.

592
00:42:07,275 --> 00:42:09,235
Mi-young, do you know
who Carl Sagan is?

593
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:12,238
- Carl Sa...
- <i>Cosmos</i>, that really thick book.

594
00:42:12,321 --> 00:42:14,866
- Oh, yes. Right.
- The universe is infinitely vast.

595
00:42:14,949 --> 00:42:17,118
And it's expanding at a fast pace.

596
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:18,953
There really could be

597
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:22,665
UFOs out there somewhere.

598
00:42:23,791 --> 00:42:25,918
Oh, I see.

599
00:42:26,002 --> 00:42:30,048
We can't rule out the chance
that aliens exist.

600
00:42:30,673 --> 00:42:32,759
They could literally be
watching us right now.

601
00:42:32,842 --> 00:42:35,344
- Goodness.
- Doesn't that blow your mind?

602
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:36,637
My gosh!

603
00:42:37,680 --> 00:42:40,433
Don't you find the whole idea
of what's normal

604
00:42:40,516 --> 00:42:43,978
way too Earth-centric?

605
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:47,523
I mean, what do humans look like

606
00:42:48,274 --> 00:42:49,859
from an alien's point of view?

607
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:51,402
Speaking of which...

608
00:42:51,986 --> 00:42:54,822
- Why don't we go stargazing tonight?
- Stargazing...

609
00:42:54,906 --> 00:42:57,742
<i>My aunt was fully ready</i>
<i>for a new romance</i>

610
00:42:58,159 --> 00:43:00,745
<i>but she decided to swear off love</i>
<i>for the time being.</i>

611
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:03,164
What a cursed life.

612
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:11,672
<i>And I finally got my hands</i>
<i>on an ordinary relationship</i>

613
00:43:11,756 --> 00:43:13,800
<i>completely free</i>
<i>from anyone else's meddling.</i>

614
00:43:15,176 --> 00:43:16,761
Ms. Gong, I'm here.

615
00:43:17,637 --> 00:43:18,721
Hey.

616
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:24,227
- Looks like you're almost done.
- Hardly.

617
00:43:24,519 --> 00:43:25,853
I've only just begun.

618
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:28,564
When am I going
to sort through all this?

619
00:43:29,315 --> 00:43:30,900
- Aren't you hungry?
- I am.

620
00:43:30,983 --> 00:43:33,194
- Since it's moving day, let's...
- I'll make you some <i>aglio e olio.</i>

621
00:43:33,486 --> 00:43:34,779
No, I want <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>

622
00:43:35,655 --> 00:43:36,864
Wait.

623
00:43:37,323 --> 00:43:41,285
No, please.
Let's just get <i>jjajangmyeon.</i>

624
00:43:41,369 --> 00:43:42,578
You don't like <i>jjajangmyeon?</i>

625
00:43:42,662 --> 00:43:43,996
<i>Jjajangmyeon?</i>

626
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:49,877
This is lube.

627
00:43:50,336 --> 00:43:51,712
If you look here...

628
00:43:52,004 --> 00:43:53,297
Try touching it.

629
00:43:55,591 --> 00:43:56,717
Hello.

630
00:43:57,009 --> 00:43:58,511
Is it your first time
at a place like this?

631
00:43:59,178 --> 00:44:01,180
- I see. Then...
- Go ahead and feel it.

632
00:44:01,264 --> 00:44:04,016
We've recently updated our packaging.

633
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:09,230
Go take a breather if you're tired.

634
00:44:09,772 --> 00:44:11,023
No, we're far too busy.

635
00:44:11,107 --> 00:44:13,192
- Let's grab good food afterward.
- What are we having?

636
00:44:13,484 --> 00:44:14,569
Beef.

637
00:44:15,486 --> 00:44:18,364
Hey, why would you
third-wheel a date?

638
00:44:18,447 --> 00:44:20,032
I haven't been getting enough meat

639
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:21,576
since our boss stopped
going on blind dates.

640
00:44:21,659 --> 00:44:23,703
- Let's all go together later.
- No.

641
00:44:25,872 --> 00:44:26,914
Eat without us.

642
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:31,127
- Okay, thanks.
- Thank you.

643
00:44:31,210 --> 00:44:33,212
Let's go to our usual place.

644
00:44:42,221 --> 00:44:43,389
Is it perhaps

645
00:44:44,557 --> 00:44:46,142
your first time
using a product like this?

646
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:48,603
Well...

647
00:44:48,686 --> 00:44:49,687
Yes.

648
00:44:50,646 --> 00:44:54,066
These two are
highly recommended for first timers.

649
00:44:54,609 --> 00:44:58,404
This one uses air circulation,
so it's gentle.

650
00:44:58,487 --> 00:45:00,406
And this one has
refined intensity levels.

651
00:45:00,489 --> 00:45:04,702
I see. Then, which one's better?

652
00:45:06,078 --> 00:45:08,247
Have you tried them yourself?

653
00:45:09,874 --> 00:45:11,792
<i>And then, I realized.</i>

654
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:14,670
<i>What does sex even mean to you?</i>

655
00:45:14,962 --> 00:45:17,340
<i>Why do you have</i>
<i>such a narrow view of sex?</i>

656
00:45:17,715 --> 00:45:20,218
<i>That there was actually no answer</i>
<i>to the question</i>

657
00:45:20,301 --> 00:45:23,221
<i>I'd had this whole time.</i>

658
00:45:23,304 --> 00:45:25,181
I'll go with this one.

659
00:45:25,806 --> 00:45:27,350
Sure, I'll bag that up for you.

660
00:45:28,643 --> 00:45:29,894
Thank you.

661
00:45:39,028 --> 00:45:42,615
<i>The answer always changes</i>

662
00:45:42,698 --> 00:45:44,909
<i>based on the experiences</i>
<i>I fill my life with.</i>

663
00:45:49,288 --> 00:45:51,707
It's been forever
since we last came here.

664
00:45:52,625 --> 00:45:55,294
You once told me
that one can never predict

665
00:45:55,378 --> 00:45:57,171
how a relationship might unfold

666
00:45:58,172 --> 00:45:59,757
and look at what has become of us.

667
00:46:00,716 --> 00:46:02,093
You've won, Ms. Gong.

668
00:46:03,135 --> 00:46:04,136
I'm sorry?

669
00:46:04,804 --> 00:46:08,808
That day I first looked
into your eyes...

670
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:12,812
You're finally looking at my eyes.

671
00:46:13,980 --> 00:46:17,566
I think my feelings for you started
right then and there.

672
00:46:21,529 --> 00:46:24,240
Should we call it a tie, then?

673
00:46:26,575 --> 00:46:29,412
Because for me,
it started on that day.

674
00:46:30,621 --> 00:46:32,665
<i>The day we first kissed.</i>

675
00:46:45,970 --> 00:46:46,971
That being said

676
00:46:47,972 --> 00:46:51,142
I want to try something
I've never considered

677
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:53,769
doing before.

678
00:46:55,438 --> 00:46:56,480
What?

679
00:47:03,446 --> 00:47:04,447
Ms. Gong.

680
00:47:05,865 --> 00:47:07,783
What are you doing?

681
00:47:07,867 --> 00:47:09,702
Hold on.

682
00:47:09,785 --> 00:47:10,911
I mean...

683
00:47:15,624 --> 00:47:17,043
You're aware.

684
00:47:17,585 --> 00:47:20,421
I have no intention of marrying yet.

685
00:47:21,881 --> 00:47:26,302
I'm so incredibly happy
with our relationship as it is.

686
00:47:27,011 --> 00:47:28,929
I don't want to ruin this moment

687
00:47:29,555 --> 00:47:32,224
over some convention like marriage.

688
00:47:33,267 --> 00:47:35,436
You understand me, right?

689
00:47:39,106 --> 00:47:40,649
These are just matching rings.

690
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,987
I only mean to try for matching rings

691
00:47:45,237 --> 00:47:46,572
which I've never considered
in my life.

692
00:47:47,156 --> 00:47:49,241
I love the idea. Matching rings.

693
00:47:52,370 --> 00:47:53,371
Let me put it on you.

694
00:47:57,833 --> 00:47:59,335
How is it? Does it fit?

695
00:48:08,135 --> 00:48:09,136
Wait.

696
00:48:19,063 --> 00:48:20,231
It's beautiful.

697
00:48:21,816 --> 00:48:22,942
It really is.

698
00:48:29,698 --> 00:48:31,450
Look at you.

699
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:34,870
- I've never done this.
- Really?

700
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:37,206
Come.

701
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:42,420
- This one.
- All right. Perfect.

702
00:48:42,503 --> 00:48:43,838
Oh, it's taking the picture.

703
00:48:44,338 --> 00:48:46,465
- Like this?
- No, like this.

704
00:48:46,549 --> 00:48:47,675
You've got to pose like this.

705
00:48:52,304 --> 00:48:53,556
There.

706
00:48:54,515 --> 00:48:55,641
<i>What the?</i>

707
00:48:56,058 --> 00:48:57,059
<i>No way!</i>

708
00:48:57,685 --> 00:48:58,853
<i>You read my mind, didn't you?</i>

709
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:01,147
<i>Right? You read my mind.</i>

710
00:49:22,710 --> 00:49:24,003
Ms. Gong.

711
00:49:24,336 --> 00:49:27,256
You look like you could land
a triple axel with your physique.

712
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:30,342
- It's quite surprising.
- The ice here is terrible.

713
00:49:30,843 --> 00:49:32,678
Let's just go sledding next time.

714
00:49:34,430 --> 00:49:35,723
See you later.

715
00:49:41,395 --> 00:49:44,732
- I'm sorry. Are you okay?
- Yes, I'm fine.

716
00:49:44,815 --> 00:49:46,358
I wasn't watching
where I was going. I'm sorry.

717
00:49:46,442 --> 00:49:47,610
It's okay.

718
00:49:49,528 --> 00:49:51,155
Babe, are you okay?

719
00:49:56,785 --> 00:49:57,786
Are you all right?

720
00:49:59,246 --> 00:50:00,414
I'm fine.

721
00:50:00,498 --> 00:50:02,458
- Shall we skate together?
- Aren't you getting hungry?

722
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:04,418
Not at all. I'm having a blast here.

723
00:50:10,216 --> 00:50:11,383
<i>Hold on tight.</i>

724
00:50:11,467 --> 00:50:13,969
<i>- Don't let go.</i>
<i>- I think I'm getting the hang of it.</i>

725
00:50:15,596 --> 00:50:17,014
<i>I think we can skate together now.</i>

726
00:50:27,775 --> 00:50:28,776
Here.

727
00:50:32,112 --> 00:50:33,906
Can I get a bite of that too?

728
00:50:34,740 --> 00:50:36,659
Of course. Here you go.

729
00:50:43,165 --> 00:50:44,291
I should've ordered that one.

730
00:50:44,375 --> 00:50:46,627
- Want to trade?
- No, I'm good.

731
00:50:50,589 --> 00:50:51,799
<i>Ms. Gong, hold on.</i>

732
00:51:03,936 --> 00:51:05,020
NO COFFEE ON AN EMPTY STOMACH

733
00:51:05,104 --> 00:51:06,355
NEVER SKIP YOUR MEALS

734
00:51:18,742 --> 00:51:20,160
<i>There was a time when I believed</i>

735
00:51:20,244 --> 00:51:22,621
<i>marriage was</i>
<i>the final destination of love.</i>

736
00:51:23,414 --> 00:51:25,040
<i>There were also days</i>

737
00:51:25,124 --> 00:51:27,710
<i>when I was paralyzed</i>
<i>by the fear of an uncertain future.</i>

738
00:51:31,213 --> 00:51:32,631
<i>You're supposed</i>
<i>to apply a generous amount?</i>

739
00:51:32,715 --> 00:51:33,716
<i>Of course.</i>

740
00:51:36,552 --> 00:51:38,929
<i>But now I know.</i>

741
00:51:40,222 --> 00:51:42,933
<i>That the butterflies I feel today</i>

742
00:51:43,017 --> 00:51:45,019
<i>will make me</i>
<i>that much stronger tomorrow.</i>

743
00:51:47,229 --> 00:51:48,772
<i>Just like our instincts knew</i>

744
00:51:48,981 --> 00:51:52,318
<i>we'd fall in love</i>
<i>during our first kiss</i>

745
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:56,905
<i>we'll just know again</i>
<i>when the time is right for marriage.</i>

746
00:51:59,158 --> 00:52:00,951
<i>And until then, we only have to keep</i>

747
00:52:01,327 --> 00:52:03,454
<i>building our present together</i>
<i>while we wait for that future.</i>

748
00:52:16,383 --> 00:52:17,551
Should I turn off the lights?

749
00:52:29,313 --> 00:52:30,314
MAKE ME TINGLE

750
00:52:30,397 --> 00:52:32,191
<i>Make me tingle.</i>

751
00:54:08,036 --> 00:54:10,038
Subtitles by Songmi You
and Eunjin Erica Kim
